  m_text: "The graphics card draws only triangles. ProBuilder keeps four-sided and larger faces for editing and splits them into triangles for drawing. The number of triangles in a model is its polycount.\n\n<b>Predict:</b> Put the three shapes in order, from fewest triangles to most.\n\n<b>Try:</b>\n1. Set the Scene view's draw mode to Shaded Wireframe: the lines now show the triangles.\n2. Count the cube's triangles.\n3. Select the cube, use ProBuilder's Triangulate, and count again.\n\n<size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: 0 \xB7 What a mesh is (this scene)</color></size>"
